<name>SRS Airbag System</name>
<para id="RM000002887012X" category="C" type-id="8024X" name-id="555BO-01" from="200912">
<dtccode>B1623</dtccode>
<dtcname>Airbag sensor rear RH initialization malfunction</dtcname>
<dtccode>B1632</dtccode>
<dtcname>Lost Communication with Airbag Sensor Rear Right</dtcname>
<dtccode>B1633</dtccode>
<dtcname>Airbag sensor rear RH initialization malfunction</dtcname>
<dtccode>B1642</dtccode>
<dtcname>Driver side side satellite sensor bus communication stop</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM000002887012X_01" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___000069O00001">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>The side collision sensor RH (for side airbag and curtain shield airbag deployment judgment) circuit consists of the airbag computer assembly, side airbag sensor assembly RH and airbag sensor rear RH. </ptxt>
<ptxt>The side airbag sensor assembly RH and airbag sensor rear RH detect impacts and send signals to the airbag computer assembly for airbag ignition judgment. </ptxt>
<ptxt>When a malfunction is detected in the side collision sensor RH (for side airbag and curtain shield airbag deployment judgment) circuit, DTCs B1623, B1632, B1633 and B1642 are recorded in the airbag computer assembly. </ptxt>
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.00in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="3.00in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="3.08in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC No.</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC Detection Item</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Trouble Area</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B1623</ptxt>
<ptxt>B1632</ptxt>
<ptxt>B1633</ptxt>
<ptxt>B1642</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Short between terminals, open circuit, short to ground or short to +B in W/H between airbag computer assembly and side airbag sensor assembly RH</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Short between terminals, open circuit, short to ground, open circuit or short to +B in W/H between side airbag sensor assembly RH and airbag sensor rear RH</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Side airbag sensor assembly RH malfunction</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Airbag sensor rear RH malfunction</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Airbag Computer Assembly Malfunction</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
<entry>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Floor wire No.2 (between airbag computer assembly and side airbag sensor assembly RH)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Floor wire No.2 (between side airbag sensor assembly RH and airbag sensor rear RH)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Side Airbag Sensor Assembly RH</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Airbag Sensor Rear Right</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Airbag Computer Assembly</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</content5>
</subpara>
